  "1 bolted/threaded: the pivot bolt of the clamp shears (and the loose nut drops): the horn falls out of its bracket and dangles on its cable, still talking",
  "2 tied: the cable snaps at the grommet: it drops",
  "3 threaded/crimped/glazed: on the floor the bell and the can come apart, the cap comes off, the lamp breaks",
  "4 seamed/tied: the bell splits along its length, the plug rolls away, the coil and the tape wad spring out of the can, the tag goes",
  "5 bolted/strapped: the repair plate and the clamp band come off the bell",
  "6 hinged: the safety strap lets go of the bracket; 8 never in a normal break: the magnet stays in the can; the bracket stays anchored"
